+// counters.  This is also the explicit pre-capture init path: call it once per
+// device before any cudagraph capture.
+//
+// PROTOCOL VERSION 2 -- BREAKING.  `out` is an **int64**
+// CUDA tensor with EXACTLY kNumTopKExactCounters (11) elements; int32, and any
+// other length, are REJECTED rather than silently accepted.  The device counters are 64-bit unsigned
+// and are copied D2D without conversion, so the reader's element width must
+// match the device's.
+//
+// Why the break rather than a reinterpreting reader: the counters were u32
+// copied into a SIGNED int32 tensor.  At 65,536 columns with k=512 an
+// all-equal row drops 65,024 ties, so [6] goes negative in Python after 33,027
