+// signed boundary gives a wrong delta, which is worse than a missing number
+// because it looks like a measurement.  Keeping u32 and reinterpreting in the
+// reader would need an enforced per-window increment bound plus quiescent
+// resets, i.e. a contract every future caller has to remember.  64-bit device
+// counters make the failure unreachable instead: `atomicAdd(unsigned long
+// long*)` is native on sm_86 (it is a single ATOM.E.ADD.S64, not a CAS loop),
+// so the instrument costs the same, and a 64-bit slot cannot be driven to the
+// signed boundary by any run this kernel will ever see.
+//
+// The layout is the UNION of the tie-determinism and large-path slot
+// maps -- the large path's ten slots plus the decode restart's [10] decode_overflow, eleven in all,
+// with nothing renumbered.  The two switch flags are slots INSIDE the array at
+// [8] and [9], not two elements appended after it, so a probe sized to the
+// old ten- or five-element layout is rejected by the length check below rather
+// than being filled with the wrong meanings.  Ask the build for its own answer
+// with `torch.ops._C.persistent_topk_exact_counters_slots()`.
+//
+// Everything that reads these counters must move together: the Python reader
+// `vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/ops/topk_counters.py` allocates int64 and
+// eleven slots, and the medium- and large-path tests do too.  An int32 caller gets a loud
+// error rather than half a number.  The OPERATOR SCHEMA is unchanged (dtype
+// and length are not part of it), so a stale caller fails at the check, not at
+// the binding.
+//
+// Slots:
+//   [0] medium-path rows entered           (denominator)
+//   [1] rows where a 4,096-slot guard would drop a candidate
+//   [2] rows that took the exact restart   (0 in the control arm)
+//   [3] exact restarts that could not complete (must stay 0)
+//   [4] large-path rows emitted deterministically (0 in the control arm)
+//   [5] large-path rows whose pivot-equal group was cut at the k-th value
+//   [6] large-path pivot-equal elements discarded by those cuts
+//   [7] large-path invariant violations (must stay 0)
+//   [8] 1 if MERLIN_TOPK_EXACT_MEDIUM is on, else 0   (host-written)
+//   [9] 1 if MERLIN_TOPK_DET_LARGE is on, else 0      (host-written)
+//   [10] decode rows whose buffered candidates exceeded DBUF (3,708)
+//        before deterministic ranking -- MUST be read before any decode-path
+//        determinism claim
+//
+// COHERENCY -- stated precisely, because the earlier wording overclaimed.
+// With `sync == 0` the snapshot is ordered ONLY against work already enqueued
