+    only reachable through the test-only injector. Arm it for the whole
+    process: `MERLIN_TOPK_LARGE_FAULT_INJECT` is read into a function-local
+    static on the first launch, exactly like the two switches, so it CANNOT be
+    monkeypatched inside a session that has already run a top-k kernel. Run
+    this test in its own process:
+
+        export MERLIN_TOPK_DET_LARGE=1 MERLIN_TOPK_LARGE_FAULT_INJECT=1
+        pytest -k large_fault_in_nonzero_cta
+
+    Setting the injector also suppresses __trap(), so this is the trap-off arm
+    of the policy. The trap-on arm kills the CUDA context by construction and
+    belongs in a disposable-process GPU run, not here.
